From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvdisplay: conftest: require crypto_akcipher_verify() for LKCA

The libspdm glue (kernel-open/nvidia/libspdm_*.c) only compiles its real
Linux Kernel Crypto API backend when USE_LKCA is defined, which requires
both the NV_CRYPTO_PRESENT conftest result and a set of CONFIG_CRYPTO_*
options (see internal_crypt_lib.h). Otherwise every primitive is stubbed
out to return an error, which is a fully supported configuration ("It is
possible that we don't have access to all the functions..."): SPDM device
attestation is only used for confidential computing on PCIe dGPUs and is
never exercised on Tegra, where the GPU is integrated.

Upstream commit 6b34562f0cfe ("crypto: akcipher - Drop sign/verify
operations", v6.13-rc1) removed crypto_akcipher_verify(), which
libspdm_ecc.c calls in its USE_LKCA path; signature verification moved to
the separate crypto_sig API. The existing "crypto" conftest does not probe
for it -- its own comment admits "This test is not complete and may return
false positive" -- so on a kernel that enables CONFIG_CRYPTO_ECDSA and
friends (Armbian 6.18.43 does) USE_LKCA is turned on and the build dies:

  nvidia/libspdm_ecc.c:312:27: error: implicit declaration of function
  'crypto_akcipher_verify'; did you mean 'crypto_akcipher_reqtfm'?

The reference Yocto build on 6.18.22 (which also lacks the function --
it has been gone since v6.13) only succeeds because its kernel config
leaves NV_CONFIG_CRYPTO_PRESENT undefined, i.e. it silently takes the
stub path already.

Make the conftest reference crypto_akcipher_verify so that
NV_CRYPTO_PRESENT is only defined on kernels where the LKCA code can
actually compile; on newer kernels libspdm falls back to the designed
stub path. Deliberately not a LINUX_VERSION_CODE check: distro/stable
kernels backport API changes regardless of version number.

Upstream-Status: Pending [applicable to OE4T/nv-kernel-display-driver wip-r36.5-take-2]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>

diff --git a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh
index 26a737e..5ba3252 100644
--- a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh
+++ b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh
@@ -6550,6 +6550,21 @@ compile_test() {
                 struct shash_desc sd;
                 struct crypto_shash cs;
                 (void)crypto_shash_tfm_digest;
+                /*
+                 * NOTE: this CODE fragment is a double-quoted shell string,
+                 * so no double quotes may appear in this comment.
+                 *
+                 * crypto_akcipher_verify() was removed by kernel commit
+                 * 6b34562f0cfe (crypto: akcipher - Drop sign/verify
+                 * operations) in v6.13; libspdm_ecc.c depends on it, so
+                 * without it the LKCA-backed libspdm code cannot build
+                 * and must fall back to the stub implementations.
+                 * Referencing the undeclared identifier is a hard compile
+                 * error (not just -Wimplicit-function-declaration, which
+                 * conftest suppresses), so this reliably fails the test on
+                 * kernels where the function is gone.
+                 */
+                (void)crypto_akcipher_verify;
             }"
 
             compile_check_conftest "$CODE" "NV_CRYPTO_PRESENT" "" "symbols"
